rewrite_to_dnf converts an arbitrary boolean expression to disjunctive normal form:
def rewrite_to_dnf(expr: BooleanExpression) -> tuple[BooleanExpression, ...]:
    expr_without_not = rewrite_not(expr)
    return visit(expr_without_not, _RewriteToDNF())
That conversion is exponential in the worst case, and nothing bounds the size of the result. Applications that pass user-supplied filters through it can see a small input produce a very large expression.

